\subsection{The Theory Inspector}\label{subsec:theory_inspector}
To support musicians without formal training while avoiding cognitive overload, we keep the Theory Inspector closed until selected. Clicking a note builds a deterministic fact block of intervals, spacing, and rule checks, with visual warnings for violations. An on-demand chat sidebar answers contextual queries (Figure~\ref{fig:theory_inspector}): replies are retrieval-augmented from a curated theory lexicon grounded in Open Music Theory~\cite{Gotham:2021}, then phrased in plain language. Because LLMs remain unreliable at multi-step symbolic music reasoning~\cite{Zhou:2024}, the Inspector explains and suggests only; it never drafts the score. Auditor, Tutor, and Stylist personas propose alternative voicings as an ``Interpreter'' under explicit user control~\cite{Louie:2020}, ensuring no changes are written to the score without confirmation.

